[ROCm] Fix broadcast of 8-bit integers in HIP codegen

LegalizeSafeMemoryAccess adds a zero else-branch to a dynamically indexed copy,
and binds the zero to a variable. For uint8 vectors, HIP's Broadcast then failed
in one of two ways:

- 4 lanes: ICHECK(p) on as_const_int, since the value is a variable.
- 8 and 16 lanes: make_uint2/make_uint4 with one argument per byte, for example
  "no matching function for call to 'make_uint4'" with 16 arguments.

Vectors of 8-bit integers are stored as 32-bit words, so emit one packed word
per 4 lanes, for constant and non-constant values. The output for a constant
4-lane broadcast is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/rocm/codegen/codegen_hip.cc b/src/rocm/codegen/codegen_hip.cc
